1. Kotlin Basics — Hello World, Employee Bonus, and Digit Average (Exp 25)
2 marks
Write Kotlin programs for three tasks:

(1) print "Hello Kotlin!!!";

(2) compute an employee bonus based on dept_code and years of experience — define at least three departments with different bonus rules (e.g., IT + >5 yrs → 20%, HR + >3 yrs → 15%, others → 10%) and display the computed bonus amount using the when expression;

(3) read an integer from user input and compute and display the average of its individual digits.

2. Function Declarations — Default, Named, Vararg, and Higher-Order (Exp 26)
4 marks
Write a Kotlin program demonstrating four types of function declarations:

(1) a function with at least two default parameters — call it with and without providing those defaults;

(2) the same or another function called using named arguments (passing arguments out of order);

(3) a function with vararg to accept a variable number of Int arguments and print them all; and

(4) a higher-order function that takes a lambda (Int) -> Int as a parameter and applies it to a list of integers.

3. Student Class — Properties, Constructors, and Methods (Exp 27)
4 marks
Define a Kotlin class named Student with properties: rollNo (Int), name (String), course (String), and percentage (Double).

Use a primary constructor to initialize all properties.

Add two member functions: one to accept/update student data from user input, and one to display all details in a formatted manner.

Apply appropriate access modifiers.

Instantiate at least two Student objects in main() and call both functions on each.


